# Text interface: the house text HIG (text-hig skill). pacman prints this text
# as it is and cannot colour or prompt, so it is plain lines of at most 80
# columns, with the commands to copy set apart by four spaces.
post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'

macbook91-cs4208 is installed. Apply the card policy and reboot:

    systemctl --user restart wireplumber
    sudo reboot

Then check the result. The verifier asks a few questions, prints one PASS or
FAIL and, on failure, writes a single diagnostic archive:

    macbook91-audio-verify

What the WirePlumber rule does, and why it is not optional

  Software volume. The internal speaker path has no hardware volume control,
  so without the rule the volume slider does nothing and output stays at full
  scale. macbook91-audio-verify reports a FAIL if the rule did not take effect.

  Its own ACP profile set. This card has exactly one usable analog output
  profile, and the stock profile set drops that profile's only port while
  headphones are plugged in: the desktop then shows "Dummy Output" and there
  is no sound at all, from speakers or headphones. The driver moves the stream
  to the headphone converter itself, so the port must stay.

  The speakers appear as a 4-channel device ("Analog Surround 4.0"): the four
  internal amplifiers sit on four TDM slots, measured as two stereo pairs
  rather than a surround layout. Stereo content is copied to both pairs, so it
  reaches all four amplifiers.

  Speakers survive a deep suspend, confirmed on hardware across five suspends
  in one day, the longest 1 h 44 min.

To roll back completely, remove the package and reboot:

    pacman -R macbook91-cs4208-dkms

Kernel series

MSG
    printf 'The module is built for kernels of Linux series %s.\n' \
        "$(/usr/lib/macbook91-cs4208/kernel-series --list 2>/dev/null || echo '(unknown: the series list could not be read)')"
    cat <<'MSG'
DKMS skips every other kernel, which keeps its stock codec and has no speaker
output. After every kernel installation a warning names each installed kernel
of another series. Boot the LTS kernel for audio until the package supports
that series.

The CachyOS LTS kernel (linux-cachyos-lts) is the default this package depends
on. Install linux-cachyos-headers to have the module built for the current
CachyOS kernel as well.

MSG
}

# Deliberately the same message: an upgrade shows what an installation shows.
# (Replacing the package's early name macbook91-cs4208 is a removal plus an
# installation, so post_install runs then; measured in an isolated pacman root.)
post_upgrade() { post_install; }
